# Line endings
#
# Several files in this repository were committed with CRLF and later converted
# to LF inside ordinary behaviour commits, which buried a handful of real edits
# in ~1700 lines of diff noise and made the change effectively unreviewable.
# Declaring the intent here means the conversion happens once, on checkout and
# check-in, instead of depending on whichever editor touches a file next.
#
# text=auto lets Git decide what is text; eol=lf pins the working-tree ending so
# it is the same on Linux, macOS, and Windows. Normalize the existing tree with:
#
#     git add --renormalize .
#
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: never examined for text, never converted.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.xlsx binary
*.hex  binary
*.bin  binary
*.elf  binary

# Tabular data read by gimbal.cpp's lookup tables. Text, but keep it LF so the
# transcribed values stay diffable against the source sheet.
*.csv text eol=lf
